GOLDEN RULE — READ BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE
================================================================================

YOU MUST NEVER MODIFY ANY FILE THAT EXISTS IN THE YCODE REPO.

The Ycode files are:
→ app/(builder)/ycode/** — the entire builder
→ app/(site)/** — the site renderer
→ lib/** — all utilities
→ components/** — all components
→ stores/** — all Zustand stores
→ hooks/** — all hooks
→ types/** — all types
→ database/migrations/** — all migrations
→ proxy.ts — the middleware
→ next.config.ts — Next.js config
→ tailwind.config.ts — Tailwind config
→ package.json — dependencies

WHAT YOU CAN DO:
→ Create NEW files in NEW folders
→ Import from Ycode files (read-only)
→ Create new API routes in app/qay/ folder
→ Create new pages in app/(qay)/ folder
→ Add new env variables
→ Add new packages via npm install
→ Create new DB tables (never alter Ycode's)
→ Override UI-only things via CSS variables

WHY:
→ Ycode releases updates (v1.2.1 now, v1.3 later)
→ If you never touch their files, git pull = instant upgrade
→ All QAY features live in your folders only

THE FOLDER STRUCTURE WE ARE CREATING:
/app
  /(qay)          ← QAY auth pages (login, signup, dashboard)
  /qay            ← QAY-specific pages (landing, pricing, help)
  /api/qay/       ← QAY API routes (billing, client, analytics)
  /client/        ← Client mode dashboard
  /(builder)/ycode/  ← UNTOUCHED Ycode builder
  /(site)/           ← UNTOUCHED Ycode site renderer

/qay              ← All QAY code lives here
  /components/    ← QAY components
  /lib/           ← QAY utilities
  /styles/        ← QAY theme overrides (CSS only)
  /types/         ← QAY type extensions

HOW YCODE AUTH WORKS (critical to understand):
→ Ycode has a "welcome wizard" at /ycode/welcome
→ The wizard connects a Supabase project
→ It runs migrations, creates the first user
→ Auth is handled by Supabase Auth
→ proxy.ts checks auth on /ycode/* routes
→ useAuthStore manages the auth state

QAY'S APPROACH:
→ We use the SAME Supabase project as Ycode
→ We add OUR tables on top (qay_ prefix)
→ We add OUR auth pages that feed into the
  same Supabase Auth that Ycode uses
→ When a QAY user logs in, they can access /ycode
→ Site isolation is enforced by our qay_sites table

