THE ISOLATION STRATEGY:
Ycode is a single-project editor (one Supabase project = one workspace).
To give each developer isolated sites:
→ Each qay_site has its own ID
→ We pass ?siteId=UUID to the Ycode editor URL
→ The editor uses this siteId to scope all queries
→ All Ycode API calls that take a page/layer/collection
  ALREADY use site context from their DB schema
→ RLS in Supabase enforces user = owner

Since Ycode's migrations use a flat schema (no site_id
per user — it's designed for one workspace), our approach:
→ Use qay_sites as the site directory
→ Each qay_site maps to a "project" in Ycode
→ The editor URL carries the site context
→ We add site_id to the /ycode route as ?site=[qay_site_id]

